  "inferenceRules": [
    "Weapon families are not expected to perform equally against every defense; the study seeks coherent niches and meaningful costs rather than convergence toward universal 50-percent matchups.",
    "Kinetic candidates should be evaluated especially against Armor-exposed/Armor-heavy targets, while poor Shield-heavy performance can be healthy family identity rather than automatic imbalance.",
    "Energy reference lanes are controls for family identity, not a target that Kinetic or Missile candidates must numerically match.",
    "Missile GP warheads may mature by energetic generation; specialist warheads should coexist with contemporary GP payloads and should not be required to rescue an obsolete GP packet.",
    "Normal Kinetic/Missile variants use generic magazine accounting; rare exotic individually tracked ammunition is outside CP115.",
    "Kinetic saturation retains one battery attack roll; increased coverage is represented by an accuracy bonus, while a successful attack package may resolve multiple smaller packets.",
    "Ordered/tandem Kinetic packets resolve sequentially within one attack package and one hit roll; CP115 does not introduce extra attacks per battery.",
    "Controlled target fixtures exist only to expose characteristic niches and are never legal-build or production-promotion gates.",
    "Adaptive Missile pairing may use only observer-safe Firm-track combat assessment and never hidden Shield/Armor values.",
    "No CP115 outcome automatically changes CP109/CP110 numbers, Concept rules, Storyboard technology placement, or production C#/Godot runtime."
  ]
}
